(Optional, to make this robust against the next addition: rather than maintaining a denylist of unsupported keywords, an allowlist of the *supported* keywords — `type`, `properties`, `items`, `required`, `enum`, `const`, `anyOf`, `allOf`, `$ref`, `$defs`, `description`, `format`, `additionalProperties` — fails safe when Anthropics schema surface changes. Your call; the denylist is fine if you prefer to keep the supported set permissive.)
